 ## Limitations
-Historical memory-target successes come from separate runs and do not establish identical full-training behaviour. Numerical coverage varies by case, as detailed above and in RESULTS. The latest October 30 evaluation met three of nine memory targets, below the target of six; its raw first-category matches and valid correct diagnoses are reported separately. The diagnosis-only comparison is one fixed-order pass without repeats, with two unconfirmed reference causes retained in the full denominator. Both new s2 precision-policy tests and the HF Trainer repair failed to meet their requirements; a statically accepted HF configuration edit did not establish a successful repair. Saved-snapshot analysis has produced valid diagnoses, although some explanations still contain factual errors. The web interface can analyze an explicitly shared server capture by ID using new Nebius inference; external snapshot upload is optional. Neither path runs the supplied training code or proves a GPU repair. A large public upload timed out before analysis.
